.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::NumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV_InterFace< dim >"Couples the nodes on the opposite sides of the \fBInterFace\fP, using an operand (thermal or hydraulic conductivity) and the thickness attribute "thickness" for the interface\&. (the latter needs to be defined as a separate variable with the placement INTER_FACE)\&.

.PP
The coupling is created by emulating a thin-shell element (prism or hexahedron)\&. For this purpose the opposing collocated nodes are separated from one-another an amount equivalent to the thickness before the coordinate matrix is initialised\&.

.PP
The separation of the nodes creates prism or hexahedral elements, from triangular and quadrilateral \fBInterFace\fP objects\&. The \fBInterFace\fP normal is used in the construction of the edges of these elements\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
SKM 
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
18/8/22 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV_InterFace\fP< dim >::NumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV_InterFace (const \fBModel\fP< dim > & model, const char * oper, const char * basic, const char * test)"
Constructor gets the finite element types that \fBNumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV_InterFace\fP needs to turn the \fBInterFace\fP into the equivalent of a volumetric element from the \fBFiniteElementManager\fP\&. Since InterFaces can either be triangles or quadrilaterals, their extruded volumetric pendants are prism and hexahedral elements\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
the variable 'thickness' needs to be defined on the \fBInterFace\fP, else the pde operator will not work\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV_InterFace\fP< dim >::ComputeContribution (const \fBInterFace\fP< dim > & iface)\fR [final]\fP, \fR [override]\fP"
Computes integral over shape function derivatives squared\&. These are the shape functions of the volumetric elements that match the lower-dimensional \fBInterFace\fP\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
The connections could also be established using line elements, but this would require a more complicated accumulation process\&.
.RE
.PP
