.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::NumIntegral_dNT_op_dN_dV_InterFace\fP< dim >::InitialiseCoordinateMatrix (const \fBInterFace\fP< dim > & iface, \fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & XYX) const\fR [protected]\fP"

.PP
separates opposing nodes and writes new coordinates to XY matrix of corresponding finite element type Spatially separates opposing nodes in the direction of the unit normal of the \fBInterFace\fP\&. It follows that the extrusion direction is perpendicular to the \fBInterFace\fP and the extrusion amount is given by the \fBInterFace\fP "thickness\&. The method writes the new coordinates to the XY matrix of the \fBInterFace\fP cell, following the node numbering convention of the corresponding (resulting) prism or hexahedral element\&.

.PP
\fBTodo\fP
.RS 4
Before using this in computations test that the finite element swap works and that the node numbering of the contribution matches that of the prism or hexa\&. 
.RE
.PP


